 "notes": [
  "THE TALENT TREE (client/scenes/pages/talents_page.gd). Every rect is measured off the painting's own gold.",
  "The three columns stand at x 185, 467 and 749; the five medallions at y 608, 797, 981, 1166 and 1352. One template, fifteen instances, each knowing its branch and its place in it.",
  "A medallion's state is drawn OVER the painting: the ring crop (lit or plain) covers the painted ring and puts five empty sockets under it, and a lit gem is laid on each rank the lord has bought. The painting lights its top two rows; a lord's tree is its own.",
  "'medallions' below says WHICH talent stands on which painted medallion, because the icons mean something: the sword is Sharpened Steel, the brazier is The Night Watch, the clover is A Lucky Hand. A talent the list does not name falls back to the branch's own order, so a new one in balance/talents.json cannot break the page.",
  "The one band that may stretch is the six rows of bare ground between the columns' pointed feet (which end at 1483) and the button bar's rail (1492). It has to be BELOW every medallion: the medallions are drawn as live nodes over the painting, and a band between two of them would move the painting's own medallion out from under the one drawn on top of it. Those rows are levelled flat in art/slices/talents.json, because six rows drawn forty high show every grain as a streak."
 ],
